// $Id$

// Here I have what should be a complete list of names for Unicode
// characters as of late 2026. It maked such an absurdly long file that at
// present I do not intend to use it, but it is here for reference. 

// This file has been created by looking at the UnicodeData file that
// gives official information on all codepoints and keeping just the
// items that have general class M*.

// The full table has over 40000 entries. It seems that clang can compile
// it without apparent effort, but g++ uses a LOT of memory. So much that
// I have split the table into 4 parts each in a separate file. Even with
// around 10000 entries in each table I find that on an ARM Linux  with
// g++16 memory occupancy (including use of swap space) grows to o little
// around 25 GB while compiling this. 

#include "wvs.h"

